    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/University-assistant-predoctoral/1435403633/": {
      "title": "University assistant predoctoral",
      "description": "University assistant predoctoral Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » University assistant predoctoral The University of Vienna is a community of almost 11,000 individuals, including approximately 7,700 academic staff members, who passionately pursue answers to the profound questions that shape our future. They represent individuals driven by curiosity and a relentless pursuit of excellence. With us, they find the space to try things out and unfold their potential. Are you inspired by their passion and determination? We are currently seeking a/an University assistant predoctoral 40 Faculty of Historical and Cultural Studies Job vacancy starting: 02/01/2027 | Working hours:  30.00  | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 Grundstufe (praedoc) Limited contract until: 01/31/2030, with an option to extend for one year (see \"Contract duration\") Job ID: 6196 As one of Europe’s largest research institutions, the University of Vienna offers an exceptionally broad range of subjects and, as such, an outstanding infrastructure for transdisciplinary research in the humanities. Your personal sphere of influence: The Department of Prehistory and Historical Archaeology is advertising a position (predoctoral University assistant to Prof. Thomas Kühtreiber) in the field of settlement and landscape archaeology of the Middle Ages and the modern era. The position is closely linked to the ongoing research programme ‘Dynamics in Rural Areas’ being conducted by the Chair of Historical Archaeology. Your future tasks: The pre-doctoral research assistant is expected to participate in ongoing research projects and to develop a doctoral thesis on settlement dynamics in Eastern Austria during the second millennium AD, with a particular focus on the phenomenon of abandoned villages. The integration of landscape archaeological methods and experience with GIS applications are prerequisites for this. Participation in research, teaching and administration: involvement in research projects Contribution to publications / academic articles / lecturing A dissertation proposal is expected to be finalised within 12 months Participation in, and independent delivery of teaching modules in accordance with the provisions of the collective agreement Student supervision Participation in the organisation of meetings, conferences and symposia Participation in departmental, teaching and research administration This is part of your personality: Successful candidates must hold a Master’s degree in Prehistory and Historical Archaeology or a related discipline. They must have knowledge of settlement and landscape archaeology from the medieval and modern periods, demonstrated through relevant training or practical experience (e.g. a Master’s thesis on a relevant topic, participation in a field school or work on a relevant research project) Initial experience in the interpretation of complex settlement finds at the micro- and macro-levels, including the analysis of small finds, would be an advantage Knowledge of Geographic Information Systems (preferably QGIS) is desirable During the initial period, proficiency in German (C1) must be demonstrated; written and spoken English (B2) forms an important basis for the work. Initial experience in academic project work is an advantage What we offer: Contract duration : The employment duration is 3 years . Initially limited to 1.5 years, the employment relationship is automatically extended to 3 years if the employer does not terminate it within the first 12 months by submitting a declaration of non-extension. With appropriate work progress, an extension to a total maximum of 4 years is possible. Fair salary : The monthly gross salary is 3.836,10 € (on a full-time basis, 14x/year) and it increases if we can credit professional experience. Work-Life-Balance: The position is for 30 hours per week. You will have flexible working hours and may also work remotely on a part-time basis. We place great importance on a high degree of flexibility in working hours, particularly with regard to applicants’ care responsibilities. Inspiring working atmosphere: We offer the opportunity to work within an international and interdisciplinary team drawing on a range of theoretical and methodological approaches and research traditions. Good public transport connections : Your workplace in the center of beautiful Vienna is easily accessible by public transport. The place of work is Vienna, unless you are traveling for research and conference purposes. A workspace in a shared office will be provided. Internal further training : We continuously offer you opportunities to expand and deepen your skills, including through participation in the Doctoral School of Historical and Cultural Studies (DSHCS) . Equal opportunities for all : We welcome every additional personality to the team! It is that easy to apply: Applications can be submitted in German or English and must include letter of motivation (max. 2 pages) CV a brief outline of a phD-project (max. 2 pages) Master-Thesis Leaving certificates further documents, if necessary. If you have any questions, please contact: Thomas Kühtreiber thomas.kuehtreiber@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities , the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection ​Application deadline: 10/31/2026 Prae Doc Apply now » Find similar jobs: predoctoral, Praedoc, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary)  prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimizing video performance, or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing, and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising Cookies Provider Description Enabled AddThis Google Analytics is a web analytics service offered by Google that tracks and reports website traffic. Cookie Information Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider AddThis Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
