    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/University-assistant-predoctoral/1445876333/": {
      "title": "University assistant predoctoral",
      "description": "University assistant predoctoral Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » University assistant predoctoral The University of Vienna is a community of over 10,000 individuals, including approximately 7,500 academic staff members, who passionately pursue answers to the profound questions that shape our future. Fueled by curiosity and a deep sense of duty, they contribute invaluable insights to research and teaching, enriching our society. Are you inspired and driven by the desire to make a meaningful impact? We are currently seeking a/an University assistant predoctoral 37 Faculty of Business, Economics and Statistics Job vacancy starting: 11/16/2026  | Working hours:  30.00  | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 Grundstufe (praedoc) Limited contract until: Job ID: 6266 Conduct research and teach at the University of Vienna, where more than 7,500 academics thrive on curiosity in continuous exploration and help us better understand our world. Does this sound like you? Then join our accomplished team! Your personal sphere of influence: The Research Unit Technology and Innovation Management , part of the Department of Accounting, Innovation and Strategy , conducts research covering the emergence, development, and commercialization of new ideas and inventions. We try to better understand how various incentive mechanisms, different forms of organizing as well as characteristics of individuals and organizations and their environment influence their innovation activities. The topics of courses offered are aligned with these research topics and are mostly targeting master students. The project We are expanding the Bürokratieindex (Bureaucracy Index) a data-driven measure of the volume of German federal legislation, measured in standard pages of consolidated legal text. The index shows that the body of federal law has grown by more than 60% since 2010, with no legislative period reversing the trend. The next phase is about breadth. The successful candidate will help extend the data infrastructure along three dimensions: Coverage and comparison — EU legislation, building equivalent indices for other countries, so that levels and growth rates can be compared internationally Measurement — moving beyond text volume toward indicators that capture what the text actually does such as Restrictiveness indicators : counting binding language — shall, must, may not, is prohibited, is required to — to distinguish obligation-creating text from definitions, transitional provisions and boilerplate Cross-reference network complexity : treating the legal corpus as a citation network between statutes and individual provisions, and using network statistics (degree distributions, path lengths, clustering, community structure, centrality of individual norms) to measure how entangled the body of law has become over time — an approach applied to the US Code and to German federal law, but not yet linked systematically to economic outcomes Amendment churn : how often provisions are changed, and how much of the annual growth is new regulation versus rewriting of existing rules Sectoral incidence : mapping regulatory text to industries so that burden can be matched to firm-level data The longer-term research agenda asks how regulatory burden interacts with innovation — patenting, firm entry, R&D investment, and technology adoption. The employment duration is 4 years . Initially limited to 1.5 years, the employment relationship is automatically extended to 4 years if the employer does not terminate it within the first 12 months by submitting a non-extension declaration. Your future tasks: You actively participate in research, teaching & administration, which means: Build and maintain automated pipelines that collect legal texts from national and EU sources Develop and validate the measures above, and test which ones actually predict economic outcomes Link regulatory data to firm-, patent- and industry-level datasets Conduct empirical analysis and co-author papers for international peer-reviewed journals We expect you to finalize your dissertation agreement within 12-18 months. You work on the completion of your doctoral thesis You hold courses independently within the scope of the provisions of the collective bargaining agreement. This is part of your personality: Completed Master's degree or Diploma in economics, management, data science, law, computational social science or a closely related field completed by the start date Genuine interest in the intersection of law and economics, and in how regulation shapes innovation Strong quantitative and data-management skills; proficiency in R and/or Stata, and SQL Experience with web scraping and crawling is highly relevant — a substantial part of the work involves building the data yourself (links to a GitHub profile or a scraping/NLP project you have built are welcome) Experience with natural language processing (text classification, embeddings, LLM-based extraction) is a strong plus; familiarity with network analysis is welcome Ability to work independently, and excellent written and spoken English (C1 level) What we offer: Work-life balance: Our employees enjoy flexible working hours and can partially work remotely. Supervision by Prof. Stefan Wagner and integration into an active research group . Good public transport connections: Your workplace is easily accessible by public transport. Internal further training & Coaching: Funding for conference travel, data and computing resources, and the opportunity to deepen your skills on an ongoing basis.  There are over 600 courses to choose from – free of charge. Fair salary: Employment under the University of Vienna collective bargaining agreement, including social insurance, with a basic salary of EUR 3.776,10 (on a full-time basis) increases if we can credit professional experience. Work on a novel, publicly visible dataset with considerable impact. It is that easy to apply: With your scientific curriculum vitae (see Guidelines ) Motivation letter (see Guidelines ) Master's Degree  /  Diploma Master's transcripts Via our  job portal/ Apply now -  button If you have any questions, please contact: Stefan Wagner stefan.wagner@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities, the advancement of women and diversity . We lay special emphasis on increasing the number of women in senior and in academic positions among the academic and general university staff and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection ​Application deadline: 11/08/2026 Prae Doc Apply now » Find similar jobs: predoctoral, Praedoc, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary)  prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimizing video performance, or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing, and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising Cookies Provider Description Enabled AddThis Google Analytics is a web analytics service offered by Google that tracks and reports website traffic. Cookie Information Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider AddThis Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
